id: CLI-A11Y-021
ilities: [accessibility]
source: cpm
maturity: 4
action: advisory
title: CLI project without man page
category: a11y
severity: info
engine: file-absence
target:
  filenames: man
  # A real man page is a roff file with a section-number extension (.1 for
  # user commands). file-absence treats filenames and extensions as OR, so a
  # committed man/cpm.1 satisfies the rule even though its basename is not
  # literally "man". The .1.md pandoc source alone is not enough — ship the
  # generated roff so `man cpm` works.
  extensions: .1
fix: "Add a man page (man/tool.1). Generate it from a markdown source with pandoc if you like (man/tool.1.md -> pandoc --to man). Screen reader users have specialized scripts for reading man pages — the standardized format is more accessible than --help output."
